{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>who delivered you from the hand of Egypt and from the hand of Pharaoh</b> — For He performed a great sign for you, in that Pharaoh and his people did not kill you, even though on your account great plagues came upon them in their land. And this sign was great for Moses as well; therefore he mentioned it to him included in the whole, saying \"you\" — meaning you and the people. And there is yet another sign: <b>who delivered the people from under the hand of Egypt</b> — for they were in Egypt and came out from there to eternal freedom. And R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra] said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 18:10) that he blessed first, \"Blessed be HaShem who delivered you\" — meaning you and Aaron, through whom the plagues came upon Pharaoh and upon Egypt — and afterward he blessed, <b>who delivered the people from under the hand of Egypt</b>, in Egypt and at the Sea."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:09.271624526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}